llama: load only the output-head rows of a token list

The head is one matmul over every vocabulary row, and Ling-3.0 has 157,184 rows, most of them never used on the
packs' text. llama_model_params::head_rows loads only the listed rows; decode scatters their logits into the full
array and leaves the rest at -1e30. llama_head_extra_tokens adds the current prompt's tokens outside the list, with
their logits computed from their own rows in the file, so a source can still be quoted. Pixel 10, Ling, 97,168 rows:
decode +7.4% (docs/BENCHMARKS.md).

